positive extra: class_id == expected_classification == as_filed_class_id; expected_leak_rule None; leak_kind "none"; axis_vector in-vocab.
negative: class_id None; expected_verdict "reject"; expected_leak_rule in catalog.

Checks by leak_kind for negatives:
- axis: axis_vector present and in-vocab; resolve(axis_vector) != [as_filed]; if expected_classification in class_ids: resolve == [expected_classification]; if expected_classification=="NO_CLASS_IN_TAXONOMY": resolve == [].
- out_of_vocabulary: violated_vocabulary non-empty; each entry has axis/value/allowed; value not in allowed (and axis in vocabulary keys); axis_vector may be null.
- lexical: axis_vector in-vocab and resolve == [as_filed] (or for composite as_filed not a class → skip resolve requirement, require violated_vocabulary); pattern = case.get("text_pattern") or catalog rule pattern; require re.search(pattern, statement) — if no pattern in catalog and no case pattern → error.
- semantic: semantic_witness non-empty; either (axis_vector in-vocab and resolve==[as_filed]) or (violated_vocabulary non-empty); if forbidden_tokens_absent then require none of them present in statement (confirming paraphrase).

Also generic checks: duplicate case_id; counts; coverage; all four classes covered by positives and negatives (for negatives, "covering" means as_filed_class_id or expected_classification or the class of the axis vector — for global composites there's no class; I'll count a negative as covering class C if C in {as_filed_class_id, expected_classification, resolve(axis) entries}).

Wait: N13/N14/N15/N16 are global; N01 covers vacuum WCC via as_filed; etc. Coverage per class for negatives: WCC-VAC: N01,N02,N03,N17 (4); SCC-C2: N04,N05,N06,N18 (4); SCC-C0: N07,N08,N09,N16 (4); SCALAR: N10,N11,N12 (3). Good.

Controls: implement `mutate_cases(cases, control_id)` returning mutated list; run `check_corpus` and assert expected error code present.

Error codes: use short strings prefixed to messages, e.g., "POSITIVE_NOT_SINGLE_CLASS", "NEGATIVE_CLEAN_MEMBER", "COVERAGE", "DUPLICATE_CASE_ID", "UNKNOWN_LEAK_RULE", "VOCAB".

Report structure:
```json
{"verdict":"PASS","taxonomy_sha256":..., "cases_sha256":..., "catalog_sha256":...,
 "counts":{"positive":16,"negative":18,"total":35},
 "coverage":{"positive":{cls:4...},"negative":{cls:...}},
 "machine_verified":{"axis_cases":N,"out_of_vocabulary_cases":N,"lexical_cases":N},
 "semantic_pending":[...case_ids],
 "errors":[],
 "controls":[{"control_id":"C1",...,"expected_error":"...","detected":true}],
 "disjointness_ok":true, "unique_axes_per_class":true}
```
Exit 0 iff errors empty and all controls detected.

Also stdout human summary.

